The Zong population was reduced by the internment policy, the staged riot of October 1941, and wartime conditions. The "Other" category declined from 6% to 4%, reflecting both the loss of Zong internees and the departure of Volisanian military personnel after 1946.

=== Urbanisation ===

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Year !! Urban !! % !! Rural !! % !! Notes
|-
| 1935 || ~245,000 || 58% || ~185,000 || 42% ||
|-
| 1947 || ~250,000 || 55% || ~203,000 || 45% || Urban decline from bombing. Rural shift as war production collapsed.
|}

[[Waribá]], damaged by the firebombing of 1945, experienced a population decline. The famine of 1946 produced a rural shift as displaced industrial workers returned to subsistence agriculture.

